hadiths[15]{hadithnumber,text}:
"16069","Ismail ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, he said, Muhammad ibn Ishaq informed us, he said, Said ibn Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq narrated to me, from his father, from Sahl ibn Hunayf, he said, I would meet hardship from madhiy, and I would bathe much from it, so I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about that, and he said: Ablution suffices you of it. So I said, how about what touches my garment, and he said: It suffices you to take a handful of water and wipe with it of your garment where you see it touched."
"16070","Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, he said, al-Amash narrated to us, from Abu Wail, he said, Sahl ibn Hunayf said, accuse your opinion, for we saw ourselves on the day of Abu Jandal, and had we been able to repel his affair, we would have repelled it, and by Allah, we did not put our swords from our shoulders since we accepted Islam for an affair that horrifies us, but it made easy for us to an affair we know, except this affair, we did not close an opponent but another opponent opened for us."
"16071","Yala ibn Ubayd narrated to us, from Abd al-Aziz ibn Siyah, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, he said, I came to Abu Wail in the mosque of his people, asking him about these people whom Ali killed at al-Nahrawan, in what they obeyed him, and in what they parted from him, and in what he deemed their fighting lawful. He said, we were at Siffin, and when killing intensified among the people of Syria, they took refuge on a hill, and Amr ibn al-As said to Muawiyah, send to Ali with a codex, and call him to the Book of Allah, for he will not refuse you. So a man came with it and said, between us and you is the Book of Allah, have you not seen those given a share of the Book, called to the Book of Allah to judge between them, then a party of them turns away, and they are averse. And Ali said: Yes, I am most worthy of that, between us and you is the Book of Allah. He said, so the Kharijites came to him, and we were calling them that day the reciters, and their swords upon their shoulders, and they said, O Commander of the Faithful, what do we await of these people upon the hill, shall we not walk to them with our swords until Allah judges between us and them. So Sahl ibn Hunayf spoke and said, O people, accuse yourselves, for we saw ourselves on the day of al-Hudaybiyah, meaning the truce that was between the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the polytheists, and had we seen fighting, we would have fought. So Umar came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, O Messenger of Allah, are we not upon truth, and they upon falsehood, are not our slain in Paradise, and their slain in the Fire. He said: Yes. He said, then why do we give vileness in our religion, and return, while Allah has not judged between us and them. So he said, O Ibn al-Khattab, I am the Messenger of Allah, and He will never waste me ever. He said, so he returned, enraged, and did not have patience until he came to Abu Bakr, and said, O Abu Bakr, are we not upon truth, and they upon falsehood, are not our slain in Paradise, and their slain in the Fire. He said: Yes. He said, then why do we give vileness in our religion, and return, while Allah has not judged between us and them. So he said, O Ibn al-Khattab, he is the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Allah will never waste him ever. He said, so the chapter of Victory was revealed. He said, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Umar, and had him recite it to him. He said, O Messenger of Allah, and is it a victory. He said: Yes."
"16072","Yazid ibn Harun narrated to us, he said, al-Awwam informed us, he said, Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani narrated to me, from Yusayr ibn Amr, from Sahl ibn Hunayf, he said, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The tribulation of a people before the east, shaven their heads. And he was asked about Madinah, and he said: Sacred, secure, sacred, secure."
"16073","Abu al-Nadr narrated to us, he said, Hizam ibn Ismail al-Amiri narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq al-Shaybani, from Yusayr ibn Amr, he said, I entered upon Sahl ibn Hunayf, and I said, narrate to me what you heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the Haruriyyah. He said, I narrate to you what I heard, I will not add to it for you, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioning a people emerging from here, and he pointed with his hand toward Iraq, reciting the Quran, not passing their throats, passing through religion as the arrow passes through the game. I said, did he mention a mark for them. He said, this is what I heard, I will not add to it for you."
"16074","He said, Yunus ibn Muhammad and Affan narrated to us, they said, Abd al-Wahid, meaning Ibn Ziyad, narrated to us, he said, Uthman ibn Hakim narrated to us, he said, my grandmother al-Rabab narrated to me, and Yunus said in his hadith, she said, I heard Sahl ibn Hunayf saying, we passed by a stream, and I entered and bathed from it, and I came out fevered, and that was reported to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: Order Abu Thabit to seek refuge. I said, O my master, and spells are good. He said: No spell except in a soul, or fever, or sting. Affan said, the evil eye, and the sting, and the fever."
"16075","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, he said, Malik narrated to us, from Abu al-Nadr, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, that he entered upon Abu Talhah al-Ansari visiting him. He said, so we found with him Sahl ibn Hunayf. He said, so Abu Talhah called a man and removed a mat from under him. So Sahl ibn Hunayf said to him, why do you remove it. He said, because in it are images, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said about them what you knew. Sahl said, did he not say, except what is a figure in a garment. He said: Yes, but it is better for my soul."
"16076","Husayn ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said, Abu Uways narrated to us, al-Zuhri narrated to us, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, that his father narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out, and they went with him toward Makkah, until when they were at the ravine of al-Khazzar of al-Juhfah, Sahl ibn Hunayf bathed, and he was a white man, handsome of body and skin, and Amir ibn Rabiah, brother of Banu Adi ibn Kab, looked at him while he was bathing, and said, I never saw as today, nor the skin of a secluded maiden. So Sahl was struck down, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought to, and it was said to him, O Messenger of Allah, have you concern for Sahl, by Allah, he does not raise his head, nor does he recover. He said: Do you accuse anyone of him. They said, Amir ibn Rabiah looked at him. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called Amir, and was severe upon him, and said: Upon what does one of you kill his brother, had you, when you saw what pleases you, invoked blessing. Then he said to him: Wash for him. So he washed his face and his hands and his elbows and his knees and the ends of his feet and the inside of his waist-wrapper in a cup, then that water was poured upon him, a man pouring it upon his head and his back from behind him, tipping the cup behind him. So that was done with him, and Sahl went with the people, with no harm in him."
"16077","Ishaq ibn Isa narrated to us, Mujammi ibn Yaqub al-Ansari narrated to me at Quba, he said, Muhammad ibn al-Kirmani narrated to me, he said, I heard Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf saying, my father said, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever goes out until he comes to this mosque, meaning the mosque of Quba, and prays in it, it is like the recompense of an umrah."
"16078","Qutaybah ibn Said narrated to us, he said, Mujammi ibn Yaqub al-Ansari narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Kirmani, he said, I heard Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, and he mentioned the like of it. He said."
"16079","Ali ibn Bahr narrated to us, he said, Hatim narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Sulayman al-Kirmani narrated to us, and he mentioned its meaning."
"16080","He said, Rawh and Abd al-Razzaq narrated to us, he said, Ibn Jurayj informed us, he said, Abd al-Karim ibn Abi al-Mukhariq narrated to me, that al-Walid ibn Malik ibn Abd al-Qays informed him, and Abd al-Razzaq said, of Abd al-Qays, that Muhammad ibn Qays informed him that Sahl informed him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him, he said: You are my messenger to the people of Makkah, say, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me, he conveys peace to you, and orders you with three: do not swear by other than Allah, and when you relieve yourselves, do not face the qiblah, nor turn your backs to it, and do not cleanse with a bone, nor with dung."
"16081","He said, Hasan ibn Musa narrated to us, he said, Ibn Lahiah narrated to us, he said, Musa ibn Jubayr narrated to us, from Abu Umamah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said: Whomever a believer is humiliated before, and he does not aid him, while he is able to aid him, Allah, mighty and majestic, humiliates him before the heads of creatures on the Day of Resurrection."
"16082","He said, Zakariyya ibn Adi narrated to us, he said, Ubayd Allah ibn Amr informed us, from Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil, from Abd Allah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, from his father, he said, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever aids a striver in the path of Allah, or a debtor in his hardship, or a contractee in his ransom, Allah shades him in His shade, on a day when there is no shade but His shade."
"16083","He said, Yahya ibn Bukayr narrated to us, he said, Zuhayr ibn Muhammad narrated to us, he said, Abd Allah ibn Muhammad ibn Aqil narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, that Sahl narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever aids a striver in the path of Allah, or a debtor in his hardship, or a contractee in his ransom, Allah shades him in His shade, on a day when there is no shade but His shade."
